  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi></math> and <math> <mi>z</mi> </math> be positive real numbers. Suppose <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi></math> and <math> <mi>z</mi> </math> are the lengths of the sides of a triangle opposite to its angles <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Y</mi></math> and <math> <mi>Z</mi> </math>&nbsp;respectively. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>tan</mi><mfrac><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>tan</mi><mfrac><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>,&nbsp;then which of the following statements is/are TRUE?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>Z</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>Z</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>tan</mi><mfrac><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#8722;</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>z</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B",
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>We have,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>tan</mi><mfrac><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>tan</mi><mfrac><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo></math>perimeter of a triangle&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>Apply half-angle formula and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></math>&nbsp;then,&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mo>&#8710;</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mo>&#8710;</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mi>s</mi></mfrac><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#8710;</mo><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mo>&#8710;</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>90</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>Z</mi></math></p><p>An option&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>B</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is correct.</p><p>Now,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mi>X</mi></mstyle></mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mi>Y</mi></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mo>+</mo></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mi>sin</mi></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mi>Z</mi></mstyle></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mi>sin</mi><mi>X</mi></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mfenced></mstyle></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>sin</mi><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi>cos</mi><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>tan</mi><mfrac><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>An Option&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>C</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is correct.</p>"
  }
